  {
   "id": "g-notes-programRequirements",
   "label": "Additional program requirements",
   "category": "Liberal ed",
   "sourceRef": "program",
   "rule": {
    "id": "r-notes-programRequirements",
    "type": "review",
    "sourceRef": "program",
    "message": "All degree-seeking students must complete the University\u2019s Liberal Education requirements .\nAt least 22 upper division credits must be taken at the University of Minnesota Twin Cities campus.\nCollegiate Requirements:\nAll CFANS undergraduate students must complete an Experiential Learning (EL) requirement. Experiential learning is a way to learn by doing, or learn by experiencing. Instead of acquiring information from a classroom lecture or book, experiential learning gives you active, hands-on experience in the real world. Examples of experiential learning options within CFANS include: off-campus study programs, field-based research, service-learning classes, internships, volunteer work related to your studies, and more.\nAll CFANS undergraduate students must complete an Interdisciplinary (ID) Learning Requirement. An interdisciplinary (ID) course addresses issues from at least two different academic disciplines (two fields/departments within the university). By integrating two disciplines into one class, students have the opportunity to develop integrated problem-solving skills.\nTo determine which of your major classes fulfill the EL and ID requirements, see your APAS report. Students are encouraged to work with their academic advisor to identify EL and ID requirements in their graduation planning. Verify this requirement with your advisor or APAS."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "g-notes-programAdmissionRequirements",
